# ZSoftly Capstone Project

### Stateless Web Application on AWS ECS Fargate

A containerised, stateless web application deployed on **AWS ECS Fargate** and provisioned using **Terraform**.

The project demonstrates practical implementation of **Docker containerisation, Amazon ECR, AWS networking, Infrastructure as Code, ECS Fargate, load balancing, security, monitoring, and DNS**.

---

# 1. Project Structure

```text
z-softly-capstone-project-1/
│
├── application/
│   ├── Dockerfile
│   ├── nginx.conf
│   ├── page1.html
│   └── page2.html
│
├── terraform/
│   ├── main.tf
│   ├── networking.tf
│   ├── security-groups.tf
│   ├── alb.tf
│   ├── ecs.tf
│   ├── ecr.tf
│   ├── dns.tf
│   ├── variables.tf
│   └── outputs.tf
│
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
```

### Application

Contains the Nginx web application, Dockerfile, and static pages.

### Terraform

Contains the AWS infrastructure configuration.

### README.md

Project architecture, deployment, and implementation documentation.

---

# 2. Application

The application is a lightweight **stateless Nginx web service** exposing two endpoints:

```text
/page1
/page2
```

The application does not maintain local user state, allowing multiple container instances to serve requests independently.

### Container

```text
Base Image: nginx:alpine
Port:       80
Container:  zsoftly-nginx
```

---

# 3. Docker Containerisation

The application was first containerised locally using Docker.

### Dockerfile

```dockerfile
FROM nginx:alpine

COPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/nginx.conf

COPY page1.html /usr/share/nginx/html/page1.html

COPY page2.html /usr/share/nginx/html/page2.html

EXPOSE 80

CMD ["nginx", "-g", "daemon off;"]
```

### Build the image

```bash
cd application

docker build -t stateless-app:v1 .
```

The resulting image is:

```text
stateless-app:v1
```

### Run locally

```bash
docker run --name stateless-app -d -p 80:80 stateless-app:v1
```

### Test the application

```text
http://localhost/page1
http://localhost/page2
```

This validates the application and container before deployment to AWS.

---

# 4. Amazon ECR

After validating the Docker container locally, the image is stored in **Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR)**.

### Repository

```text
zsoftly-capstone-web
```

### Image

```text
zsoftly-capstone-web:v1
```

### Authenticate Docker with ECR

```bash
aws ecr get-login-password --region eu-west-2 | \
docker login \
--username AWS \
--password-stdin 258063471393.dkr.ecr.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com
```

The ECR image is then used by the ECS task definition.

---

# 5. AWS Infrastructure

The AWS environment is provisioned using **Terraform**.

### AWS Region

```text
eu-west-2
```

### VPC

```text
10.0.0.0/16
```

The infrastructure contains:

* 2 public subnets
* 2 private subnets
* Internet Gateway
* NAT Gateway
* Elastic IP
* Route tables
* Security groups
* Application Load Balancer
* ECS Fargate
* ECR
* IAM
* CloudWatch

---

# 6. Network Architecture

```text
                         Internet
                            │
                            ▼
                  Application Load Balancer
                            │
             ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
             │                             │
             ▼                             ▼
      Public Subnet 1               Public Subnet 2
             │                             │
             │
        NAT Gateway
             │
             ▼
      Private Subnet 1             Private Subnet 2
             │                             │
             ▼                             ▼
      ECS Fargate Task              ECS Fargate Task
             │                             │
             └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                            ▼
                           Nginx
```

The Application Load Balancer is deployed in the public subnets.

ECS Fargate tasks are deployed in private subnets and do not receive public IP addresses.

---

# 7. Infrastructure as Code

Terraform is used to provision and manage the AWS infrastructure.

### Terraform workflow

```bash
cd terraform

terraform init
terraform validate
terraform plan
terraform apply
```

Terraform manages:

```text
VPC
├── Public Subnets
├── Private Subnets
├── Route Tables
├── Internet Gateway
├── NAT Gateway
└── Elastic IP

Security
├── ALB Security Group
└── ECS Security Group

Application
├── Application Load Balancer
├── Target Group
└── Listener

Compute
├── ECS Cluster
├── ECS Service
└── ECS Task Definition

Supporting Services
├── ECR
├── IAM
└── CloudWatch
```

Terraform state is stored remotely in Amazon S3.

---

# 8. Amazon ECS Fargate

The application is deployed using **Amazon ECS with AWS Fargate**.

### ECS Cluster

```text
zsoftly-capstone-cluster
```

### ECS Service

```text
zsoftly-capstone-service
```

### Task Definition

```text
zsoftly-capstone-task
```

### Configuration

| Configuration  | Value    |
| -------------- | -------- |
| Launch Type    | Fargate  |
| Tasks          | 2        |
| CPU            | 256      |
| Memory         | 512 MB   |
| Network Mode   | `awsvpc` |
| Container Port | 80       |
| Public IP      | Disabled |

The two ECS tasks run in private subnets across two Availability Zones.

---

# 9. Application Load Balancer

The Application Load Balancer provides the public entry point for the application.

```text
Internet
   │
   ▼
ALB :80
   │
   ▼
Target Group
   │
   ├── ECS Task 1
   │
   └── ECS Task 2
```

### Configuration

```text
Name:         zsoftly-capstone-alb
Protocol:     HTTP
Port:         80
Target Type:  IP
```

### Health Check

```text
Path:     /page1
Protocol: HTTP
Port:     80
Matcher:  200-399
```

Only healthy ECS tasks receive traffic from the ALB.

---

# 10. Security

The application uses a private-service architecture.

### ALB Security Group

Allows:

```text
TCP 80
Source: 0.0.0.0/0
```

### ECS Security Group

Allows:

```text
TCP 80
Source: ALB Security Group
```

Therefore:

```text
Internet
    │
    ▼
   ALB
    │
    ▼
 ECS Tasks
```

The ECS tasks cannot be accessed directly from the public internet.

Additional controls include:

* ECS tasks have no public IP addresses.
* Dedicated IAM execution role for ECS.
* ECR image scanning enabled.
* ECR encryption enabled.
* CloudWatch logging enabled.

---

# 11. DNS

The production domain is:

```text
www.leonels-projects.co.uk
```

DNS is managed through **IONOS**.

The `www` record points to the AWS Application Load Balancer.

```text
www.leonels-projects.co.uk
            │
            ▼
        IONOS DNS
            │
            ▼
   AWS Application Load Balancer
            │
            ▼
       ECS Fargate
```

> The original assignment specified Route 53. IONOS is used in this implementation because the project domain is managed through IONOS.

---

# 12. Monitoring & Logging

ECS container logs are delivered to **Amazon CloudWatch**.

### Log Group

```text
/ecs/zsoftly-capstone
```

### Retention

```text
30 days
```

### ECS Monitoring

Container Insights is enabled on the ECS cluster.

This provides visibility into:

* ECS service activity
* Running tasks
* Container performance
* Application logs
* Task failures

