# 15. Application Verification

### Local

```text
http://localhost/page1
http://localhost/page2
```

### AWS Load Balancer

```text
http://<ALB-DNS-NAME>/page1
http://<ALB-DNS-NAME>/page2
```

### Production

```text
https://www.leonels-projects.co.uk/page1
https://www.leonels-projects.co.uk/page2
```

### ECS Service

The service is configured with:

```text
Desired Tasks: 2
```

The ALB health check verifies:

```text
/page1
```

before routing traffic to a task.

---

# 16. Resilience

The application is designed to maintain service availability through:

* Two ECS Fargate tasks
* Two Availability Zones
* Application Load Balancer
* Automated ECS task replacement
* ALB health checks
* Private application subnets
* Stateless application design

If an ECS task becomes unhealthy, the ALB removes it from service while ECS can replace the task.

> **Current limitation:** The environment uses a single NAT Gateway. A fully production-grade multi-AZ design would typically deploy a NAT Gateway in each Availability Zone to remove the NAT Gateway as a single-AZ dependency.

